nina_onboard: quick heads-up — a user hit two different errors depending on their setup: `Cannot use import statement outside a module` and `client.generate is not a function`. They were following our quickstart which uses `import Redwood from '@redwood/inference'`. Any short clarifications we can add to onboarding?

sam_sdk: common story. Edge/modern apps should use ESM `import` (preferred). Node CJS apps need a compatibility pattern. Suggest three labelled snippets in docs: Preferred (ESM), Compatibility (CJS require guard), Troubleshooting (Jest/ts-jest + package.json exports).

kevin_tests: snippets i'd add:
// Preferred (ESM)
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });

// Compatibility (CJS)
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference').default || require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_KEY });

and a one-liner test for CI: `expect(typeof client.generate).toBe('function')` to catch default vs named mismatches.

emma_devex: dev docs: call out package.json `type` = "module" effects, and show an `exports` map that provides both `import` and `require` targets, e.g. `{"import":"./dist/index.mjs","require":"./dist/index.cjs"}`. Also add TS notes: `esModuleInterop: true` or `module: 'ESNext'` and `allowSyntheticDefaultImports: true`.

sam_sdk: for Jest/ts-jest include this troubleshooting snippet: use `extensionsToTreatAsEsm` + `transform: { '^.+\\.tsx?$': ['ts-jest', { useESM: true }] }` or run jest with `--experimental-vm-modules` on older Node. Mention `transformIgnorePatterns` if third-party libs are ESM.

nina_onboard: nice. Can we add a tiny debug helper in sample-app that tries require then logs a hint? something like: `try { const m=require('@redwood/inference'); console.log('require ok, hasDefault=',!!m.default); } catch(e){ console.log('require failed: you may be in ESM runtime; try import or adjust jest config'); }`

emma_devex: yes. i'll draft a PR to add: labelled examples, TS tips (including `import type { ... }` usage for type-only imports), the debug script, and an FAQ entry explaining the `.default` symptom and resolution. I'll also note that the require guard is a compat workaround, not the recommended flow for edge/modern Node.

docs-bot: please link the PR to `/docs/sdk/js/imports.md` and `/sample-app/README.md` and reference CI job `ci/sample-app/import-matrix`. Also include the one-line assertion comment for the CI test.

sam_sdk: tiny wording nit: call the CJS snippet "Compatibility (Require fallback)". Otherwise LGTM.

emma_devex: thanks everyone — i'll ping for reviews once the PR is up. If anyone has a customer repro log drop it here and i'll include it in the FAQ. :wave:
